#: src/output-files.md:1
msgid "Output Files"
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:3
msgid ""
"Output files can be provided with `[cache(outputs = FILES)]`, where `FILES` "
"is an expression that is evaluated with recipe arguments in scope and whose "
"evaluated elements are paths. Paths may be absolute or relative to the "
"recipe’s working directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:8
msgid ""
"After an invocation, the current state of outputs is recorded in the "
"invocation’s cache entry. This includes whether they are files or "
"directories, and for files, the BLAKE3 hash of their contents."
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:12
msgid ""
"All outputs must exist and match their recorded state in the cache entry for "
"an invocation to be skipped, and after an invocation runs successfully, it "
"is an error if any outputs do not exist."
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:16
msgid ""
"In this example, `build` re-runs whenever `main` is missing or modified, and "
"errors if it runs without producing `main`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:19
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set unstable\n"
"set lists\n"
"\n"
"[script]\n"
"[cache(inputs = [\"lib.c\", \"main.c\"], outputs = \"main\")]\n"
"build:\n"
"  cc lib.c main.c -o main\n"
"\n"
"clean:\n"
"  rm -f main\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/output-files.md:32
msgid "This forces `build` to re-run if `main` is deleted by `clean`."
msgstr ""
